    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>(Prerequisite: Ravenloft Campaign)</em></p><p>Something unnatural is always watching you, in the shape of scurrying vermin and other eerie creatures. You gain the following features.</p><p><strong>Borrowed Eyes.</strong> @UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.spells.Item.Aas6i0uCFP6uag7H]{Beast Sense} and @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSpeakwithA]{Speak with Animals} are always prepared for you. You can cast each of them without a spell slot, and you must finish a Long Rest before you can cast it this way again; you can also cast them with spell slots of the appropriate level you have.</p><p><strong>Heightened Suspicion.</strong> Whenever you take the Search action, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to any ability check you make as part of that action.</p><p><strong>Incessant Watchers.</strong> You have Disadvantage on saving throws against the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplScrying000]{Scrying} spell. In addition, immediately after you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test, paranoia threatens to overwhelm you. Make a Wisdom saving throw (DC 13 plus your Proficiency Bonus). On a failure, you have Disadvantage on D20 Tests for 1 minute. You can repeat the save at the end of each of your turns, ending the effect on a success.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-WmDBBGhLPmmdV5GD\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Heightened Suspicion</em> rolls the 1d4 to add to the check. <em>Incessant Watchers</em> is a Wisdom saving throw against DC 13 + your Proficiency Bonus; on a failure, apply its effect (Disadvantage on D20 Tests, not automated).</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
